WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.610
Do you have a Brother color
changer stashed away somewhere?

2
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.820
Now is a great time to pull
it out and give it a try.

3
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.460
I have to admit, I've never used a color

4
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.540
changer before,
and I was really stumped

5
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.100
by the instruction book
for installing this thing.

6
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.860
But with a little perseverance,
I conquered it.

7
00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.660
Let me share.

8
00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:31.220
Before you get as frustrated as I did,
do a little research and confirm that your

9
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.780
color changer can be
used with your machine.

10
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:40.220
I discovered after a whole lot of fussing
and fuming that this model is KCC.

11
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:46.560
Model color changer is not compatible
with my Brother bulky 260.

12
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.580
Now, if you don't have a manual for your

13
00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:56.380
color changer, you should be able to find
it in our free manuals and documents page.

14
00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.660
Now, I had a printed manual
and it's on the cover.

15
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.900
It said it's model KCC.

16
00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:09.820
And doing a little research, this appears
to be the same as the KHC 820 manual.

17
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.380
This is a single bed

18
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:16.920
color changer.
Can't be used with the ribber.

19
00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:24.340
I was able to connect my new toy
to my brother 970 by using the KHC arm

20
00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:27.980
connector that comes
with the color changer.

21
00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:31.700
This allows me to keep
my ribber in place.

22
00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:34.700
The color changer device itself is held

23
00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:40.540
in place on an arm that is inserted
into that connector

24
00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:46.520
and puts everything right in place
for the carriage to pick up the colors.

25
00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.260
Now, as I was connecting everything,

26
00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.540
at first I couldn't get the arm
into the connector until I realized that I

27
00:01:55.570 --> 00:02:00.140
needed to tilt it up a bit
and slip the pieces together.

28
00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.020
Lesson learned, don't force anything.

29
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:07.210
It will slip into place very easily.

30
00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.940
Once I figured all this out,
things went more smoothly.

31
00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:16.860
Included with my color changer
is a yarn tension setting stand.

32
00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.360
Now, this one had me stumped.

33
00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.660
I couldn't figure out what it was for,

34
00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:26.220
and it's a clamp that adds a place
to insert the second yarn mast.

35
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:31.220
Apparently, on the older machines,
this piece was needed.

36
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.340
Thankfully, on my 970,

37
00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:39.260
there's already a spot right in the bed
itself for that extra yarn mast.

38
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.700
Well, thankfully,
because this little stand didn't fit

39
00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:46.000
anywhere on my machine
and I don't need it.

40
00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:53.700
Following the manual once I get everything
into place, I was surprised and pleased

41
00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:59.020
to learn that it was fairly simple
to thread and use the color changer.

42
00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:03.460
Here's an overview
for working with four colors.

43
00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:08.580
First, change to the color
changer sinker plate.

44
00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:13.220
Now, along with the color changer device
with all the buttons,

45
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:17.700
this is what's really going to be
doing all the work for you.

46
00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:23.340
Now notice you have to tilt that sinker
plate to pass it over the sinker posts

47
00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.220
and slip it into place under
the knobs of your carriage.

48
00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.160
So be careful in inserting it.

49
00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:31.600
It's a little different than the others.

50
00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.740
Put two tension masts in place

51
00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:40.860
and thread up the masts with each color.
To make things easier.

52
00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:44.700
If you're using a stitch pattern
that has colors marked 1-2-3-4.

53
00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:50.420
Be sure to arrange the colors
in the color changer accordingly.

54
00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.740
Thread up each color in the color changer.

55
00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:57.500
Now, I tried to make this
harder than it really is.

56
00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:03.300
All you have to do is push in, say,
button 1, and thread the first yarn

57
00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:07.100
around the yarn guide
and in the groove of the roller.

58
00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.900
Now, you shouldn't have to struggle.

59
00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.960
The yarn pops right into place.

60
00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:14.820
Continue

61
00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:19.700
for each color,
I recommend that you peek from the back

62
00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:25.560
to make sure there's no hang ups and each
of the yarns are correctly in place.

63
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.300
When all four colors are threaded,

64
00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:53.440
loop them around and secure them
underneath the yarn holder.

65
00:04:54.480 --> 00:05:00.560
So now you have your hands free, the yarns
are threaded up, and they're secure.

66
00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:04.300
My first experiment,
I started with no needles in work.

67
00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.980
Just to keep things
really clean and simple.

68
00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:11.460
Push in button 1 and pass the carriage

69
00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.700
all the way to the left
past the turn mark.

70
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.380
In other words,
you want to pass the carriage far enough

71
00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:25.040
for the guide on the carriage to grab that
color that's pushed out by button one.

72
00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:28.100
Push your carriage back to the right

73
00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:31.780
slowly and confirm that you
picked up color 1.

74
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.420
Don't go too far right,

75
00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:37.180
we don't want to be pulling too
much tension off this yarn.

76
00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.820
Push the carriage back to the left.

77
00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:42.100
Push in button 2.

78
00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:47.580
Now remember to push that carriage as far
left as you need to to catch color 2.

79
00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:53.340
Push the carriage right and back again.

80
00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:58.400
Each time, confirm that you
picked up the right color.

81
00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:05.420
Now, when playing this way,
you want to be sure to milk the cow.

82
00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:10.060
I like to keep the tension on the colors
so the yarn doesn't loop up.

83
00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.460
As we're playing here,

84
00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:17.940
the whole experiment is to learn and get
a feel for how far past that turning mark

85
00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:23.160
you need to go to catch
the yarn in the carriage.

86
00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.940
For my first try at knitting,
I unthreaded everything.

87
00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:00.580
And just for practice,

88
00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:06.980
I changed back to my regular sinker plate
and I cast on some stitches.

89
00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:11.820
I started all over, changed
to the color changer sinker plate.

90
00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:14.060
I used the slip setting to position

91
00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:16.580
the carriage on the left
side of the knitting.

92
00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:20.500
We want the carriage
on the same side as the yarn.

93
00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:24.700
I then rethreaded the color
changer for practice.

94
00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:29.480
Make sure everything's moving
and in the right place.

95
00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.760
Be sure to disengage all four

96
00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:39.700
of the buttons and secure those yarn
tails under the yarn clip on the arm.

97
00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.900
Just like before.

98
00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.940
I pushed in one button,

99
00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:49.060
passed the carriage all the way to the far
left, far enough to engage the yarn.

100
00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:57.860
Push the carriage back and knit a few rows.
To change colors

101
00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:00.820
pass the carriage all the way to the left.

102
00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:04.060
Push in the button
to select the next color.

103
00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:06.920
Confirm that the yarn is
in position in the sinker plate.

104
00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:13.040
The right color has been chosen
and knit back.

105
00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:25.680
Knit a few rows of stripe
in the second color.

106
00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.060
There you go.

107
00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:41.340
Keep trying different colors
to get into a slow, steady rhythm.

108
00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:44.860
I did find that if I tried to knit too
quickly,

109
00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:49.860
or if I took the carriage too far past
the right side of the knitting,

110
00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:55.220
I not only distorted the stitches
on the right side, but I often got a loop

111
00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:59.940
where the yarn got caught up
in the mechanism underneath the carriage.

112
00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:02.660
So this takes practice to get the right

113
00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:08.380
rhythm and to make sure that everything's
working as you're knitting.

114
00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:10.940
Like everything else in machine knitting,

115
00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:14.700
I discovered there's an art
to using this color changer.

116
00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:21.340
You need to slow down, confirm the colors,
and just take it easy.

117
00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:27.520
It's still a whole lot faster and easier
than changing colors manually.

118
00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:30.740
Now that you've been successful

119
00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:35.100
in knitting stripes, I hope you've
been successful in knitting stripes.

120
00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:38.020
I encourage you to go back to your manual,

121
00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:41.860
the color changer manual,
and reread everything.

122
00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:46.860
I found that even though I struggled,
all the information I needed was there.

123
00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.780
I just found it difficult at first.

124
00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:56.200
Once I saw how things were supposed
to work, it got a whole lot easier.

125
00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:05.500
Now, your challenge is to master stripes,
no loops, no stitches pulled out of whack,

126
00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:09.620
and then play with multicolored
stitch patterns.

127
00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.700
So much fun.

128
00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:16.100
And this allows you to do so many things.

129
00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:21.020
Now, one thing to note with stitch
patterns is that punch card and electronic

130
00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:26.860
stitch patterns have to be reversed
for working with the color changer.

131
00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:29.380
You can see an example in my manual.

132
00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:33.820
The little teddy bear
is punched in reverse.

133
00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:38.860
Now, if you have an electronic machine,
you can just use the little reverse key

134
00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:45.580
or you'll have to punch your cards
correctly for the best results in using a

135
00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:51.500
single bed color changer
to knit in stitch pattern.

136
00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:54.700
I hope seeing a color changer in action

137
00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:58.880
helps, and I hope you have
success with your color changer.

